The library signatures in retrokit/sigs/ are byte patterns derived from:
- the run-time libraries of Open Watcom 2.0 and Open Watcom 1.9, distributed under the Sybase
  Open Watcom Public License 1.0 (https://github.com/open-watcom/open-watcom-v2);
- zlib 1.0.4, 1.1.3, 1.1.4 and 1.2.3 (zlib license), (C) Jean-loup Gailly and Mark Adler,
  compiled with Open Watcom;
- IJG libjpeg 6b, compiled with Open Watcom: this software is based in part on the work of
  the Independent JPEG Group.
retrokit/knowledge/zlib.h and libjpeg.h restate the public interfaces of those libraries.
retrokit/knowledge/win32/directx.h (generated by scripts/gen_com.py) records the DirectX
interface layouts - interface and method names, their order and parameter names, the binary
interface of DirectX - as read from the MinGW-w64 headers; the other win32/*.h restate the
documented APIs of the libraries they name.

retro-kit does not contain any game files or decompiled game code.
